### AI configured? (always works)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/meetings/ai/status

### Create meeting (no OpenAI required)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/meetings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "topic": "Project Review",
  "startTime": "2026-11-10T09:00:00Z",
  "endTime": "2026-11-10T10:00:00Z",
  "participants": [{ "email": "alice@example.com" }]
}

### List meetings (GET — not POST)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/meetings?from=2026-11-01T00:00:00Z&to=2026-12-01T00:00:00Z

### Check availability
POST http://localhost:8080/api/meetings/availability
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "participantEmails": ["alice@example.com"],
  "startTime": "2026-11-10T09:00:00Z",
  "endTime": "2026-11-10T10:00:00Z"
}

### Natural language (requires GEMINI_API_KEY + app restart)
### On Windows, corporate TLS is handled automatically (JDK cacerts + Windows ROOT).
POST http://localhost:8080/api/meetings/ai
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "prompt": "Schedule a team sync tomorrow 2pm to 3pm with alice@example.com",
  "timeZone": "Asia/Kolkata",
  "confirmSchedule": true
}
